<Base title={'What "unlock tech" means here'} description="What 'unlock tech' means at NeonKey: one site for beginners and builders, four doors and a few ground rules.">
  <article class="narrow page-head prose">
    <span class="kicker">Notes</span>
    <h1>What "unlock tech" means here</h1>
    <div class="meta"><DemoBadge /><span>Sample article for the demo site</span></div>
    <p class="lead">Tech can feel locked: jargon, paywalls, forums that assume you already know everything. NeonKey is about handing you a key instead.</p>
    <h2>Two kinds of readers, one site</h2>
    <p>If you're new, every guide starts with what you need and why each step matters. If you're experienced, you can skip straight to the commands, configs and the "when it breaks" section.</p>
    <h2>Four doors</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Unlock AI:</strong> small automations that save real time for small businesses.</li>
      <li><strong>Unlock Deals:</strong> honest picks, disclosed affiliate links, no fake ratings.</li>
      <li><strong>Unlock Skills:</strong> tutorials and hands-on homelab builds.</li>
      <li><strong>Unlock the Week:</strong> a short weekly email that's worth opening.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Ground rules</h2>
    <p>No hype and no guarantees. Clear labels when something is sponsored or an affiliate link. And when I'm still learning something, I'll say so.</p>
    <p><a href={url('/notes/')}>← Back to Notes</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
